    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM Auctioneers are delighted to present to the market No. 29 Castlerock Woods, a most attractive three-bedroom semi-detached residence nestled in the charming village of Castleconnell, County Limerick.\n\n\nThis delightful home represents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, families or those seeking a peaceful yet well-connected lifestyle. With an asking price of 370,000, the property offers bright and comfortable living accommodation in a superb location and is certain to appeal to discerning buyers.\n\n\nUpon entering, one is welcomed into a bright and spacious entrance hallway with a conveniently located guest WC. The main reception room provides an inviting space in which to relax with family or entertain guests. This elegant room benefits from a large bay window, which floods the interior with natural light, together with a solid-fuel stove that creates a warm and relaxing atmosphere.\n\nThe kitchen and dining area is conveniently located off the reception room and is well appointed, offering ample storage and workspace. This bright and practical room is ideally suited to meal preparation and family dining. French doors provide direct access to the sun-drenched rear garden, which features an attractive lawn and patio area.\n\n\nUpstairs, the property boasts three well-proportioned bedrooms, each offering generous accommodation and excellent natural light. These rooms provide considerable flexibility and are ideally suited to a growing family, guest accommodation or a home office. The main bathroom is tastefully finished and includes a bath with an overhead shower, wash-hand basin and WC.\n\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a private and enclosed rear garden with a lawn and feature patio area, providing a tranquil outdoor space where children can play or where one can enjoy alfresco dining during the warmer months. Off-street parking is available to the front of the residence, which is a valuable asset in this sought-after location.\n\n\nCastleconnell is a picturesque and hugely popular village renowned for its scenic beauty, vibrant community spirit and wonderful setting along the banks of the majestic River Shannon. The village offers an excellent range of amenities, including shops, cafés, welcoming hostelries, schools and healthcare facilities, making it an ideal location for families and commuters alike.\n\nThe property is conveniently positioned within easy reach of Limerick City and the wider region, with excellent road and rail connections providing ease of access to the University of Limerick, Plassey Technological Park and the nearby motorway network.\n\n\nNo. 29 Castlerock Woods presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a bright and spacious home in one of County Limerick`s most attractive and highly regarded villages. With its well-proportioned accommodation, private rear garden and excellent location, this property is expected to attract strong interest.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 5.04m (16'6\") x 2m (6'7\")\nTiled flooring, coving, W.C.\n\nLiving Room - 3.05m (10'0\") x 5.08m (16'8\")\nTimber flooring, bay window, solid fuel stove, coving, double doors to kitchen/dining room.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.05m (10'0\") x 5.08m (16'8\")\nTiled flooring, fully fitted units, patio door to rear garden, coving, recessed lighting.\n\nDownstairs guest bathroom\nwc, whb, tiled flooring\n\nMain Bathroom - 2m (6'7\") x 2.02m (6'8\")\nTiled flooring, wc, whb, bath, window.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.06m (10'0\") x 3.06m (10'0\")\nCarpet flooring, sliderobes, rear facing window.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.08m (10'1\") x 3.03m (9'11\")\nMaster. Carpet flooring, sliderobes.\n\nEn-suite - 1.01m (3'4\") x 2.08m (6'10\")\nwc, whb, shower with double shower tray, power shower, fully tiled,\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.05m (6'9\") x 2.03m (6'8\")\nTimber flooring,\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
